 doc/coinseries/spec.md     | 4 +---
 src/chainparamsbase.cpp    | 2 +-
 src/kernel/chainparams.cpp | 2 ++
 4 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/coinseries/manual.md b/doc/coinseries/manual.md
index d1dcf7d..efea67b 100644
--- a/doc/coinseries/manual.md
+++ b/doc/coinseries/manual.md
@@ -848,7 +848,7 @@ The consensus rules are fixed byte by byte in `doc/coinseries/spec.md` (consensu
 | Stage | Contents | Status |
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | 1 | Five coins, reward schedule, per-chain money limit | Done |
-| 2 | RandomX proof of work, five-chain merged mining (180-byte header) | Done (RandomX version 1 or 2 still to choose) |
+| 2 | RandomX proof of work, five-chain merged mining (180-byte header) | Done (RandomX version 1 decided) |
 | 3 | Per-block difficulty (2-hour half-life), stall relief, 10-minute future limit | Done (start difficulty to be measured on the launch laptop) |
 | 4 | Replay protection (chain identifier in every signature hash) | Done |
 | 5 | Snapshot verification and claims (BIP-322 / legacy signed message) | Done (real 840,000 snapshot to be downloaded and verified) |
diff --git a/doc/coinseries/spec.md b/doc/coinseries/spec.md
index 3f2cefd..c23c6c7 100644
--- a/doc/coinseries/spec.md
+++ b/doc/coinseries/spec.md
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ Values marked **(placeholder)** are fixed before launch; values marked **(undeci
 2. Merge tree with 8 leaves. Leaf s holds the commitment of the chain whose merge slot is s; unused leaves are 32 zero bytes. Inner node = `SHA256d(left || right)`.
 3. A chain recomputes root `M` from its own commitment at its own slot and the three siblings in the header.
 4. RandomX key `K = SHA256("coin-series/randomx" || LE64(floor(nTime / 1209600)))` — a new key every 2 weeks, derived from the header time only.
-5. `pow = RandomX_v(K, M || LE64(nNonce64))`, v = RandomX version **(undecided: 1 or 2; implementation supports both)**.
+5. `pow = RandomX_v(K, M || LE64(nNonce64))`, v = RandomX version **1** (decided; version 2 is available on regtest only, via `-randomxversion=2`).
 6. Valid if `target = Compact(nBits)` is positive, not overflowing, `≤ powLimit`, and `pow` (read as a little-endian 256-bit number) `≤ target`.
 - The genesis block is fixed by hash and exempt from proof of work.
 - A commitment placed in a different slot yields a different root; one solution can make at most one block per chain.
@@ -139,6 +139,4 @@ The txid covers version, all inputs, all outputs and lock time; input amounts an
 
 ## 12. Open items
 
-- RandomX version 1 or 2.
-- Start target and powLimit (measured on the launch laptop).
 - Bitcoin reference height H.
